   246	    Apply each row bar's own-length period across the separator, painting blanks and carving holes in solid blocks.
   247	
   248	    Input structure:
   249	    - The background is black.
   250	    - A near-solid vertical separator column splits the grid into two sides.
   251	    - One side contains one or two horizontal monochrome bars on some rows; the other side contains several solid monochrome rectangles on black.
   252	
   253	    Rule:
   254	    - Find the separator column, then identify which side contains the row bars and which side contains the solid blocks.
   255	    - For each bar of length L, look along the same row on the opposite side at separator-relative offsets L, 2L, 3L, ... until leaving the grid.
   256	    - If a sampled cell is black, paint it with the bar color; if it lies inside a solid block, change it to black.
   257	    - When a row has multiple bars, process the one closer to the separator first, and any cell already touched by an earlier bar on that row is skipped by later bars.
